    {"claim": "Absent deliberate intervention, the gains flow to whoever owns the model weights and the compute, not to the labeler in the loop.", "targets": [], "relationship": ""},
    {"claim": "Electricity took about forty years to show up in measured productivity, and Solow's 1987 line was that you see the computer age everywhere except the productivity statistics.", "targets": [], "relationship": ""}
