    {"claim": "The duty does not attach to where the entity is chartered; it attaches to the act of serving a consequential decision to a person inside the jurisdiction.", "targets": ["AN-16"]},
    {"claim": "The chartered location of the pen is not the hook; serving people here is the hook, and a captive cannot relocate the population being served.", "targets": ["AN-16", "AN-15"]},
    {"claim": "When the operator is judgment-proof, liability reaches upstream to the party that books the revenue from serving the domestic market, joint-and-several, by construction.", "targets": ["AN-15"]},
    {"claim": "A gauge that counts the misread tumor as a cost but never counts the nine thousand correct reads is a defective gauge, and I grant the refinement openly.", "targets": ["AN-17"]},
    {"claim": "Where the deployer cannot document that benefit, the one-sided floor is not over-deterrent but correct, and the attack's own logic concedes this.", "targets": ["AN-17"]},
    {"claim": "Foregone diffuse benefit is recoverable; the deskilling of a professional cohort and the erosion of institutional trust do not recover on that timescale.", "targets": ["AN-17"]}
  ],
  "key_assumptions": [
    {"assumption": "The revenue-booking party in an AI deployment licensing chain is identifiable and solvent — traceable the way tax and securities law already trace it.", "if_wrong": "If revenue attribution genuinely fragments across opaque cross-border licensing layers, the upstream joint-and-several reach loses its terminal solvent target and the captive dodge partially survives, forcing reliance on market-access denial alone rather than monetary liability."},
    {"assumption": "Deskilling of professional cohorts and erosion of institutional trust are materially harder to reverse than foregone statistical benefit from a temporarily withheld system.", "if_wrong": "If re-skilling and trust restoration turn out to be as fast as re-fielding a system, the irreversibility-asymmetry justification for weighting the downside collapses and the gauge should be symmetric."}
