  "statement_part3": "Here's where the test has to cut both ways. The Skeptic named his own exposure plainly: upstream weight-ownership has thin precedent, collective ownership doesn't scale on command, and the UBI pilots stalled. Fine — so let's apply his enforceability bar to both levers and see which one is closer to working machinery today. A usage-scaled data license has live precedent right now: publishers, image libraries, and forum platforms are signing ongoing, usage-indexed terms with model developers this year. A legislated weight-equity claim has none — there is no working precedent for a court ordering a slice of model weights handed to a labeling cohort. If 'show me enforceable bargaining power' disqualifies my appreciating stream, it disqualifies his upstream royalty harder, because mine bolts onto licensing markets that already exist and his has to be conjured from statute. Neither of us gets to assume enforcement for free. Mine is one step from existing contracts; his is several steps from anything.",
